    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d382">

                <pb facs="0382" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg266"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/760.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Special Representative of President
                    Gómez</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 15, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ferrara</hi>: In reply to your note of
                    the 13th instant, wherein you suggest that to calm the unrest of the people in
                    Cuba an additional statement be made by the American Minister at Habana
                    concerning the real attitude of the Government of the United States, I take
                    pleasure in enclosing copy of a statement<anchor n="1" xml:id="d382-f1"/> which
                    the American minister was authorized to make public yesterday.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d382-f1" n="1" xml:id="d382-f1-content">
